## ink-notes {{TAG_NAME}}

Notebook app for pen, touch and mouse on Linux (tested on Zorin OS 18 / Ubuntu 24.04).

### Highlights:
- **Sync between devices**: ☰ → Storage location puts the notebooks into a folder synced by Nextcloud, Google Drive, Syncthing or Dropbox (existing notebooks are copied, the originals stay). Changes from other devices show up within seconds while everything local is saved, conflict copies of the sync client become pages of their own, and opening a notebook that is open on another device shows a warning
- **Import from Saber**: ☰ → Import (or dragging the file into the window) now also opens Saber notebooks (`.sbn2` with its asset files next to it, `.sba` archives, old `.sbn`) – strokes with pen pressure, highlighters, shapes, typed text, images and PDF backgrounds
- **Import from Xournal++ and Rnote**: ☰ → Import (or dragging the file into the window) now also opens Xournal++ (`.xopp`, `.xoj`) and Rnote (`.rnote`) notebooks as new notebooks – strokes with pen pressure, highlighters, shapes, texts, images, paper patterns and Xournal++ PDF backgrounds; PDF pages imported in Rnote become images, infinite Rnote documents an endless notebook
- **Faster export**: PDF and PNG export and copying a selection as an image are about six times faster and PDFs are up to eight times smaller, because stroke outlines are simplified before export (at most 0.01 mm off; `INK_NOTES_EXACT_OUTLINES=1` exports every point as before)
- **Fling timing**: The swipe speed for gliding is measured with the touch screen's own event times (Wayland), so a fast swipe glides even when the lift is handled late; the fling diagnostics also report slow event handling
- **Fling fix**: A finger swipe is no longer lost when the view touches the edge of the notebook, so the page glides on after a fast swipe; the fling diagnostics (`INK_NOTES_DEBUG_FLING=1`) log moves, distance and timing
- **Feedback round**: The eraser size is set in a menu like the pens (four presets and a slider); corners of snapped triangles and polygons stay pointed; slides (landscape PDFs) get flat tiles in the page overview without an empty strip
- **Palm rejection & more feedback**: A hand resting on the screen while the pen is near is ignored (also on the title bar, no more accidental paste menu or window moving); the eraser has four sizes (button below the eraser modes, remembered); the page overview shows imported PDF pages; snapped triangles, rectangles and polygons have the same width on every side; a selection made with the pen's select button can be moved with the bare pen
- **Feedback round**: The endless canvas starts at the top left and only grows to the right and down; new text fields start short and grow with the text; toolbar buttons are larger again on small screens; on Wayland the title bar buttons (close, minimize, maximize) and moving the window work with a finger
- **View only**: 👁 in the toolbar hides the tools – pen, finger and mouse only scroll and zoom (the pen glides on like a finger), nothing can be changed by accident; tap 👁 again to write
- **Text box fix**: Ctrl+Plus/Minus now only zooms the page, no longer the whole interface as well – that made text jump to another place when leaving a text box
- **Writing fixes**: A snapped highlighter keeps its width; tips (e.g. of a "1" or of exponents) are drawn round instead of cut off, and the stroke no longer jumps when the pen lifts. Finger swipes glide more reliably
- **Faster scrolling**: A quick finger swipe keeps gliding; in the continuous view a scrollbar (opposite the toolbar, with the page number while dragging) jumps through long notebooks and PDFs; the mouse wheel scrolls twice as far. New notebooks are continuous; fixed pages are still available in the ☰ menu
- **Selection fix**: Moving, rotating and scaling large selections is smooth again and no longer maxes out the CPU (since 0.27 the selection was copied several times per frame). On the endless canvas the mouse wheel scrolls (Ctrl+wheel zooms)
- **Endless canvas**: New page arrangement "♾ Endless" – a borderless canvas to write, pan and zoom in every direction. Selectable when creating a notebook or in the ☰ menu (for notebooks with one page); the PDF export only contains the used area. New file format version 9: older app versions no longer open notebooks of this version
- **Page arrangement per notebook**: Selectable when creating a notebook – "Fixed pages" (default) or "Continuous" – and switchable later in the ☰ menu. Existing notebooks keep their previous setting
- **Pens in their color**: The pens in the toolbar appear as pens in their own color instead of a thin stroke, so they can be told apart at a glance
- **Scale images without distortion**: With the selection tool, a lock below the pen colors switches between uniform (🔒) and free scaling (🔓). Images start locked, strokes and shapes free; on a computer, the Shift key also locks
- **Smoother scrolling in large PDFs**: Newly rendered PDF pages no longer pause the display, and pages you scroll past quickly are skipped instead of rendered one after another
- **Screenshots for Flathub**: The app description (metainfo) now shows three screenshots; nothing changes in the app itself
- **Selecting with a finger**: In the selection tool, a finger selects and moves objects (on empty space it keeps scrolling); text and make space work with a finger too
- **Flatpak**: Manifest under packaging/flatpak (preparation for Flathub); exports go to the Documents folder from the user directories (e.g. ~/Documents)
- **English interface**: ink-notes follows the system language (German or English); switch it in the ☰ menu under "Sprache / Language"
- **Hold to snap**: now tolerates the slight jitter of a resting pen, so shapes also snap in the normal pen mode
- **Axis cross from two strokes**: Draw a horizontal and a vertical line crossing each other – the second one with hold or the shape tool – and both become an axis cross with arrowheads at all four ends; undo restores the first line
- **On-screen keyboard**: On GNOME/Zorin (Wayland) the on-screen keyboard now appears when tapping a name field – with finger or pen; typing and backspace work. Also, the first finger tap after using the mouse is no longer lost
- **App icon**: The window identifies itself as eu.pansi.ink-notes – the dock and taskbar show the ink-notes icon instead of a generic one (on X11 also as window icon)
- **Make space**: New tool ↕ – tap the page and drag down, everything below moves along, also on the following pages (past the end of a page it continues on the next one, missing pages are appended); dragging up closes empty space; one step for undo
- **Axis cross**: A "+" in one stroke (with hold or the shape tool) becomes an axis cross with arrowheads at all four ends; also in PDF/image export
- **Pen fix**: The first tap with the pen now registers – buttons and notebooks react immediately instead of on the second tap; strokes no longer start with a line from the previous pen position
- **Assign pen buttons**: In the ☰ menu under input, assign each pen button to erase, select, highlighter, pen or nothing (active while the button is held); buttons appear after the first press and light up green when pressed
- **Move folders**: Folders can now be moved with 📂 including their content into other folders or to the top level, like notebooks
- **Folders for notebooks**: Create, rename and delete nested folders (e.g. Semester 3 › Math) in the document manager and move notebooks with 📂; new notebooks are created in the open folder. The notebook files stay unchanged (assignment in library.json)
- **Paste with a finger**: Pressing the page with a finger for half a second opens a "Paste" menu – a screenshot, copied text or copied objects land exactly at that spot (like in Rnote)
- **Custom colors**: Every toolbar color (pens, highlighter, text) can be changed – tap it again, pick a preset or any color with 🎨; the toolbar remembers the colors. Colors on screen match the PDF/image export (black is black, the highlighter blends like in the PDF); squares and lines in the PDF are as light as on screen
- **Beta feedback II**: Four pens with their own color and width that remember changes; the highlighter no longer gets darker within one stroke and is now transparent in PDF/PNG/SVG exports too; pages seamlessly below each other with a separator line; new page via ➕ in the toolbar; delete a page in the ☰ menu (restorable); coordinate system without a gap at the origin
- **Fixes**: Renaming and deleting in the notebook manager respond again; squares, lines and dots are computed per pixel and are even at every zoom level (at least one pixel wide, anti-aliased)
- **Stroke quality**: Small loops as in "o", "a" or "e" stay round (the final stroke is built from the unfiltered pen points); stroke edges are anti-aliased (4× multisampling), round stroke ends are subdivided more finely
- **Pattern color**: Squares, lines and dots in light, medium, strong, blue or green (☰ menu, also applies to exports); dots of the dot grid on screen are as large as in the export (0.4 mm). README and documentation revised
- **Beta feedback**: Landscape PDFs (e.g. PowerPoint slides) get landscape pages without an empty strip (file format version 8); insert new pages right after the current one; the selection tool works with the pen; zoom up to 1000 % with PDF pages re-rendered more sharply
- **Text tool**: Tap the page with T and type – regular or code font, 8–36 pt, line wrapping at the box edge; move, rotate and scale text boxes like images; real, searchable text in the PDF; copied text becomes a text box with Ctrl+V (file format version 7)
- **Continuous scrolling**: Scroll through pages below each other with mouse wheel, finger or touchpad (Ctrl+wheel zooms); writing in the bottom fifth of the last page appends a new one automatically; can be turned off under ☰ → View
- **Virtual ruler**: Show and hide with L or via the toolbar; move it, rotate it by the handle (snaps to 15°); strokes along an edge become exactly straight – with pen, highlighter and shape tool
- **Partial-stroke eraser**: Remove only the part of a stroke you wipe over – one erase stroke is one undo step
- **Export & clipboard**: Current page as PNG (also transparent) or SVG; Ctrl+C also puts the selection on the clipboard as an image for chat, email or office apps
- **Page titles & table of contents**: Name pages, table of contents view in the page overview, titles become PDF bookmarks (file format version 6)
- **Import & annotate PDFs**: Open lecture slides, exercise sheets or forms as a new notebook (☰ menu or drag & drop), write and highlight on them; on export the original pages lie losslessly as vectors under the notes (file format version 5: older versions do not open such notebooks)
- **Insert images**: Screenshots via Ctrl+V, image files via the built-in file picker (Ctrl+I) or drag & drop; move, rotate, scale and write on them – also in the PDF export (file format version 4: older versions do not open such notebooks)
- **Dark mode & paper colors**: White, cream, dark gray or black; on dark paper, dark pen colors are brightened automatically (display only – files and PDF export stay unchanged)
- **Erase highlighter only**: Correct highlights without deleting the handwriting underneath – also with the pen's eraser end and side button
- **Adjustable pressure curve**: Curve from soft to hard and minimum pressure with preview, to match your own pen
- **New shapes**: Ellipses as well as arrows and double arrows drawn in one stroke are recognized (file format version 3: older versions do not open such notebooks)
- **Stable start**: No more crash when the graphics card cannot be used (e.g. missing permissions on /dev/dri); software renderer as fallback and an understandable error message
- **WSL (WSLg)**: Runs via X11 instead of Wayland under WSL automatically, because WSLg drops the Wayland connection; override with `INK_NOTES_DISPLAY=x11|wayland`
- **Important fix**: After a restart on a later page, continuing to write could overwrite the previous content of that page (affects v0.2.3 – v0.3.2)
- **New toolbar**: Narrow vertical bar with icon buttons, dockable left or right; rarely used functions in the ☰ menu, the page is centered next to it
- **Consistent dialogs**: Opaque windows without duplicate titles, page picker with thumbnails, larger controls in all popovers
- **UI usable with pen and touch**: Toolbar, popovers and dialogs now also respond to pen and finger, also with display scaling
- **Active stylus support (Lazarite / MPP / AES)**: Pen input via the Wayland or X11 tablet protocol, with pressure
- **Multi-touch touchscreen**: Zoom with two fingers, pan with one; drawing with a finger can be enabled
- **Two-stage inking model**: Smoothing while writing (1€ filter), post-processing with corner preservation when the pen is lifted
- **Geometry and shape recognition**: Lines, arrows & double arrows, rectangles, circles, ellipses, triangles, rhombuses, polygons & coordinate systems with sharp arrowheads (draw and hold); freeform strokes stay unchanged
- **Multiple notebooks**: Create, rename, delete (with trash); automatic saving in the background
- **Data safety**: Versioned file format with migration, damaged pages are set aside instead of overwritten, protection against opening twice, atomic saving
- **In-app updater**: Checks Gitea for new versions and installs them on request – only with a valid Minisign signature and over HTTPS
- **PDF export**: Strokes and shapes as vectors, for printing and sharing

### Installation:
- **Zorin OS / Ubuntu / Debian (.deb)**:
  ```bash
  sudo dpkg -i ink-notes_{{VERSION}}_amd64.deb
  ```
- **AppImage (other distributions with glibc ≥ 2.39)**:
  ```bash
  chmod +x ink-notes_{{VERSION}}_x86_64.AppImage
  ./ink-notes_{{VERSION}}_x86_64.AppImage
  ```
